# One call is yours, one waits on the caterer, and the menu day is settled
<callout icon="🧭" color="green_bg">
	The cutoff is yours to set. The second list waits on the caterer. The menu day was settled on 2026-11-18.
</callout>
## Call 1: when do orders close? <span color="yellow">**open · Sam**</span>
**Today:** orders close when the caterer phones, at about 10:45. The office places 38 orders a day.
<table header-row="true">
<tr><td>Option</td><td>Buys</td><td>What changes, and for whom</td><td>Cost</td></tr>
<tr><td>A · 10:30</td><td>The caterer gets the full list an hour before it cooks.</td><td>Staff who arrive after 10:30 miss lunch that day.</td><td>Nothing to build; one email to staff.</td></tr>
<tr><td>B · 11:00</td><td>Late arrivals can still order.</td><td>The caterer cooks from a list 30 minutes later, and asked for 45 minutes of warning.</td><td>A second call to the caterer each day.</td></tr>
</table>
<callout icon="💡" color="yellow_bg">
	**Pick (open): A.** The caterer's lead time decides it, and few orders come after 10:30. **Measure after the ruling:** count orders refused after the cutoff for two weeks. **Reverse:** if more than 1 in 10 orders is refused, move to B.
</callout>
**The caterer's lead time decides the cutoff; the late arrivals are the cost.**
## R1: does the caterer take a second list? <span color="blue">**waiting · the caterer**</span>
A refused order costs about 2 lunches a week.
<table header-row="true">
<tr><td>Option</td><td>Buys</td><td>What changes, and for whom</td><td>Cost</td></tr>
<tr><td>A · Yes</td><td>Late orders get lunch.</td><td>Sam sends two lists a day.</td><td>A fee per second list.</td></tr>
<tr><td>B · No</td><td>One list, one call.</td><td>Late orders are refused, as today.</td><td>None.</td></tr>
</table>
<callout icon="💡" color="yellow_bg">
	**Pick (waiting on the caterer): A.** It is the only option that feeds the late arrivals. **Reverse:** if the fee is over the cost of one lunch, pick B.
</callout>
**Only a second list feeds the late arrivals.**
